# Step 16: statistics, roles and variants, and where a turn's time goes.
#
# Each rule the step's done criteria name is broken here, one at a time:
# recording that never waits, nothing read at start-up, aggregates that
# rebuild to the same values, costs fixed when recorded, limits past their
# reset, ranges at day, week, month and zone boundaries, the opt-in
# refresh, the roles' fallbacks and budgets, variants per epoch, and the
# turn-time split that adds up.

[break] recording-blocks-the-loop
rule: Recording never waits: with the writer stalled and its queue full, an event is dropped and counted.
file: crates/cortex-stats/src/recorder.rs
in: Recorder::send
find: if let Err(TrySendError::Full(_)) = self.queue.try_send(message) {
replace: if self.queue.send(message).is_err() {
caught-by:
    cortex-stats::lib recorder::tests::a_stalled_writer_drops_and_counts_and_never_waits

[break] a-file-read-at-start-up
rule: Making a recorder reads nothing: the aggregates are read when they are asked for.
file: crates/cortex-stats/src/recorder.rs
in: Recorder::new
find: let (queue, receiver) = sync_channel(options.queue.max(1));
replace: let _ = crate::store::Aggregates::load(&options.dir); let (queue, receiver) = sync_channel(options.queue.max(1));
packages: cortex-stats, cortex-core
caught-by:
    cortex-stats::it store::nothing_is_read_until_it_is_asked_for
    cortex-core::it usage::a_turn_reaches_the_report_from_the_files_and_its_cost_stays_as_it_was_priced

[break] aggregates-do-not-rebuild-to-the-same-values
rule: The aggregates are each file read to its last whole line, so a rebuild from the files gives the same values.
file: crates/cortex-stats/src/store.rs
in: read_from
find: entry.offset += read as u64;
replace: entry.offset += (read as u64).saturating_sub(1);
caught-by:
    cortex-stats::it store::the_aggregates_rebuild_to_the_same_values_from_the_files
    cortex-stats::it store::two_writers_that_bring_the_aggregates_up_to_date_out_of_order_lose_nothing

[break] a-pruned-files-part-is-lost
rule: All-time totals outlive the pruning of raw files: a pruned file's part moves into what is kept.
file: crates/cortex-stats/src/store.rs
in: Aggregates::sync
find: if let Some(file) = self.files.remove(month) { self.kept.merge(&file.part); }
replace: self.files.remove(month);
caught-by:
    cortex-stats::it store::all_time_outlives_the_raw_files_and_old_days_fold_into_months
    cortex-stats::it store::the_aggregates_rebuild_to_the_same_values_from_the_files

[break] a-recorded-cost-is-priced-again
rule: A cost is fixed when it is recorded: the aggregates add the cost the record holds, never one worked out again from its tokens.
file: crates/cortex-stats/src/aggregate.rs
in: Part::add_line
find: CostBasis::Metered => sum.metered_nanos = cost.usd_nanos,
replace: CostBasis::Metered => sum.metered_nanos = (tokens.input + tokens.output * 4) * 1000,
packages: cortex-stats, cortex-core
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it usage::a_turn_reaches_the_report_from_the_files_and_its_cost_stays_as_it_was_priced
    cortex-stats::it store::all_time_outlives_the_raw_files_and_old_days_fold_into_months

[break] a-limit-past-its-reset-shown-full
rule: A limit past its reset time is reported as not known, not as full.
file: crates/cortex-stats/src/query.rs
in: current_limits
find: window.remaining = None;
replace: window.remaining = window.limit;
caught-by:
    cortex-stats::it limits::a_limit_past_its_reset_time_is_not_known_rather_than_full

[break] the-month-misses-its-first-day
rule: A calendar month runs from its first local day to today.
file: crates/cortex-stats/src/query.rs
in: days_of
find: UsageRange::Month => today.first_of_month(),
replace: UsageRange::Month => today.first_of_month().add_days(1),
caught-by:
    cortex-stats::it ranges::the_days_of_each_range
    cortex-stats::it ranges::a_range_ends_at_the_local_midnight_on_either_side

[break] the-week-starts-a-day-early
rule: A calendar week runs from its first day (Monday, or `usage.week_start`) to today.
file: crates/cortex-stats/src/query.rs
in: days_of
find: today.add_days(-back)
replace: today.add_days(-back - 1)
caught-by:
    cortex-stats::it ranges::the_days_of_each_range
    cortex-stats::it ranges::a_range_ends_at_the_local_midnight_on_either_side

[break] a-range-leaves-out-today
rule: Both ends of a range are in it: today counts.
